@startuml wiring
' LocalAiRobot — "Wiring at a glance" connection map, TOP-TO-BOTTOM power flow (1 LiPo -> ESC + buck/UPS).
' This source lives next to its render. Regenerate in place (writes wiring.png here):
'   plantuml -tpng docs/images/wiring.puml
' No Graphviz needed: !pragma layout smetana uses PlantUML's pure-Java layout engine.
' Vertical + larger fonts: no side-by-side domain boxes; the Pi's many peripherals collapse into one box.
!pragma layout smetana
top to bottom direction
hide stereotype
title LocalAiRobot — wiring at a glance (one 3S LiPo: ESC drive + buck(7.4V)/UPS to the Pi; common ground)

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam TitleFontSize 22
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontColor #333333
skinparam ArrowFontSize 15
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 12
  FontSize 18
  BorderThickness 1.5
  BackgroundColor<<io>> #DAE8FC
  BorderColor<<io>> #6C8EBF
  BackgroundColor<<model>> #FFF2CC
  BorderColor<<model>> #D6B656
  BackgroundColor<<data>> #D5E8D4
  BorderColor<<data>> #82B366
  BackgroundColor<<motor>> #F8CECC
  BorderColor<<motor>> #B85450
  BackgroundColor<<store>> #F5F5F5
  BorderColor<<store>> #666666
}

rectangle "3S 11.1V LiPo\n(single source)" as lipo <<motor>>
rectangle "ESC\n(+ BEC for servo)" as esc <<motor>>
rectangle "drive motor" as motor <<motor>>
rectangle "Adjustable buck\n(SZBK07 / XL4016)\n3S -> 7.4V, >=8A" as ubec <<motor>>
rectangle "UPS HAT\n2x 18650 (backup)" as ups <<io>>
rectangle "Raspberry Pi 5\n(+ Active Cooler)" as pi <<io>>
rectangle "PCA9685\nI2C PWM @ 0x40" as pca <<model>>
rectangle "steering servo\nDS3225 HV (ch1)" as servo <<motor>>
rectangle "Pi-powered peripherals\n(3.3V / CSI / USB-C from the Pi)\nHC-SR04P x3:  front 23/24 · left 5/6 · right 20/21\nCamera: IMX519 AF (CSI, 22->15) or a USB webcam\nFace screen:  USB-C -> /dev/ttyACM0" as periph <<data>>

' ---- power flows top -> bottom ----
lipo --> esc  : 11.1V (high current)
lipo --> ubec : 11.1V (tap)
esc  --> motor : motor drive
ubec --> ups  : 7.4V -> UPS input
ups  --> pi   : clean 5.1V (18650 backup)
esc  --> pca  : ch0: signal + V+ (ESC BEC) + GND
pi   --> pca  : 3.3V VCC + SDA/SCL (I2C)
pca  --> servo : ch1: signal / V+ / GND
pi   --> periph : 3.3V + TRIG/ECHO · CSI · USB-C

note bottom of periph
  **One 3S LiPo, two branches:** ESC (drive + servo BEC) and **buck @ 7.4V -> UPS -> Pi** (18650s buffer spikes).
  Tie **ALL grounds** together (Pi <-> PCA9685 <-> ESC <-> buck) or the PWM won't register.
  **Use an ADJUSTABLE buck set to 7.4V** (a fixed 5-6V UBEC sags ~0.5V under load -> browns the Pi 5 out).
  **PCA9685 V+ rail = the ESC BEC** (servo power), not the Pi (use an HV servo, or a separate 5-6V BEC).
  All 3 HC-SR04**P** run at 3.3V, so every ECHO is Pi-safe (no divider).
  **Jetson Orin Nano** also runs this (board HAL): same PCA9685 / servo / sensor wiring, but **physical BOARD**
  GPIO pins (not the Pi BCM 23/24 · 5/6 · 20/21 shown) and PCA9685 on **I2C bus 7** -- see config/robot.env.
end note
@enduml
